Reviewer Comments:=0A=
=0A=
Reviewer 1=0A=
Comments on revised version of Landis, "Consumption Based Responsibility fo=
r Global Warming and the Distribution of Impacts of Swiss Climate Policy"

The author responded well to the two referees' comments. The text is quite =
improved, even if it is by adding many caveats. The results are interesting=
 and deserve publication despite these caveats.
The author did not add a systematic multifactor analysis of households' cha=
racteristics explaining differences in consumption patterns and carbon foot=
prints. Nevertheless, the two-by-two decomposition in Appendix B provides s=
ome indications. It does not warrant, however, the statement of "lifetime i=
ncome to be the most important criterion for determining gwp" (line 469).=20
The introduction could be streamlined, there is quite a bit of repetition, =
e.g., the reference to results by Chancel et al. (2023) on page 2 and 3.
Points of detail:
=E2=80=A2	There are several references to Figure 3, in the text and more so=
 in Appendix B, which need to be revised now that Figure 3 changed. In Appe=
ndix B, this is used to refer to the distribution of per capita GWP by a ho=
usehold category but for all income groups confounded. This would be useful=
 alongside the distributions per income group in figures B1 to B3. I sugges=
t adding this to those figures.
=E2=80=A2	I did not carry out a systematic spellcheck, but some typos sprun=
g to my attention: "I provides" on line 213, "which" in place of "who" on l=
ine 281, "the the" on line 639, "in in" on line 950, "trasport" on line 128=
9, "decisesively" on line 1629, "sqewed" on line 1735, "or on a hypothetica=
l levy" on line 1744, "transport" on line 1787, "attenuated a somewhat" on =
line 2115.
=E2=80=A2	It would be fair to acknowledge the referees' input in the acknow=
ledgements.=0A=
